1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,980
What kind of race do the children compete in?
孩子们参加的是什么比赛？

2
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:17,670
What kind of race do the children compete in?
孩子们参加的是什么比赛？

3
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:27,490
Experiments have proved that children can be instructed in swimming at a very early age.
实验证明，儿童在很小的时候就可以接受游泳训练。

4
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,910
At a special swimming pool in Los Angeles,
在洛杉矶一个专门的游泳池里，

5
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:38,010
children become expert at holding their breath under water even before they can walk.
孩子们甚至还不会走路，就已经能熟练地在水下屏住呼吸了。

6
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:44,430
Babies of two months old do not appear to be reluctant to enter the water.
两个月大的婴儿似乎并不不愿意下水。

7
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:52,600
It is not long before they are so accustomed to swimming that they can pick up weights from the floor of the pool.
他们很快就习惯了游泳，能从池底捡起重物。

8
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:56,460
A game that is very popular with these
这些

9
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,140
young swimmers is the underwater tricycle race.
小游泳者很喜欢的一项游戏是水下三轮车比赛。

10
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:05,820
Tricycles are lined up on the floor of the pool seven feet under water.
三轮车排放在水下七英尺深的池底。

11
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:12,390
The children compete against each other to reach the other end of the pool.
孩子们互相比赛，看谁先到池子的另一端。

12
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:19,590
Many pedal their tricycles but most of them prefer to push or drag them.
许多孩子踩三轮车，但大多数宁愿推着或拉着它们走。

13
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:26,670
Some children can cover the whole length of the pool without coming up for breath even once.
有些孩子能游完整个泳池的长度，一次也不浮上来换气。

14
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:32,850
Whether they will ever become future Olympic champions, only time will tell.
他们将来能否成为奥林匹克冠军，只有时间能回答。

15
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:36,670
Meanwhile, they should encourage those among us
同时，他们应当鼓励我们当中

16
00:01:36,690 --> 00:01:40,630
who cannot swim five yards before they are gasping for air.
那些游不到五码就气喘吁吁的人。
